= Insurrection in Alto Llobregat & The Syndicalist Split

In the mining basin of Alto Llobregat (Barcelona), workers demand better working conditions and the fulfillment of the constitutional rights after a gas explosion in a mine that lead to the death of 30 miners. Next day FAI anarchists declare "libertarian communism," seizing mines, burning property registers, burning republican flags to set black flags and disarming local police. 

The government dispatches army units from near barracks suppressing the revolt within days and preparing to deport dozens of anarchist to Spanish Guinea.

This failed uprising triggers an explosive purge within the CNT. Moderate syndicalists led by Ángel Pestaña and Joan Peiró (*Los Treintistas*) denounce the FAI's "insurrectional adventurism" and demand a realistic strategy that respects democratic institutions. Pestaña is expelled from the CNT leadership and begins organizing the **Partido Sindicalista**.

